<p>Sleep is supposed to be safe, and this morning it actually is. I burrow under the blanket, chase the last threads of a dream, and pretend the day hasn't started yet.</p>

<p>The door bangs open at ten with no knock, no warning.</p>

<<dialog "Lily" "Get up loser, I need your phone charger.">>

<p>She's at my desk in a second, rummaging through the drawer, cables sliding through her fingers. I sit up, hair a disaster, blinking against the daylight she let in.</p>

<p>"Take the charger. Take whatever. Let me sleep."</p>

<p>She finds it, holds it up in triumph, and heads for the door. Pauses. Looks back at me, sleep-rumpled and irritated, and for once there's nothing to catch, nothing to catalog, nothing sparkling behind her eyes.</p>

<<dialog "Lily" "You're no fun when there's nothing to see.">>

<p>She leaves. I go back to sleep for another twenty minutes before my own guilt drags me downstairs for cereal.</p>

